  "notes": [
    "The South African identity number is modelled as thirteen digits. No source the pack cites states the format, so the scheme is a draft; the check digit is not validated. The other schemes are free text.",
    "The nine province names are read from the government's provinces page; the ISO 3166-2 codes (ZA-EC, ZA-KZN and so on) come from a secondary copy of the ISO table and are unconfirmed. The municipality is free text and no list is bundled.",
    "The twelve public holidays and the Sunday rule are read from the government's public holidays page, which states them from the Public Holidays Act 36 of 1994. The Act's own text was not fetched, so its amendments were not checked.",
    "One-off holidays (for example an election day or a day declared by the President) and school holidays are not modelled.",
    "The SARS monthly employer return (EMP201) is listed, but the due day was not found in a fetched SARS page and is a draft."
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "gov-za-holidays",
      "title": "Public holidays in South Africa: twelve days under the Public Holidays Act 36 of 1994; a holiday on a Sunday is observed on the Monday",
